sentences.l:
And as a dog, around her tender puppies standing,
a man not recognising, barks and is eager to fight,
so then within him it barked, he being indignant at the evil deeds;

but something of this kind for me the heart in my mind ponders,
how on the shameless suitors my hands I shall lay,
being alone;

Their parents indeed the gods destroyed, and they were left
orphans in the halls, and tended them heavenly Aphrodite
with cheese and sweet honey and sweet wine;

both the portion and the lack of portion of mortal men—
meanwhile the maidens the Harpies snatched away
and gave them to the hateful Erinyes to serve;
